==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kubilan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''E. Kubilan Pasalan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Kubilan Pasalan is practically a second [[Cat Cannon]] that doesn't work on Wave/Knockback Immune enemies with less range. Nevertheless, his massive reach keeps him safe and create opportunities for cheesing strategies. In long stages like [[Pitfall Zone]], however, a [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] might be useful due to his very slow attack rate.

One of his main uses is for his [[Cat Combo]] with [[Giraffe Cat]], [[Longnecks (Combo)|Longnecks]], as "Worker Cat Start Lvl UP (M)" for just 2 units is very convenient, as it is a slot-efficient Worker Cat Start Lvl UP combo and can be paired up with [[Don't Mess With Me! (Combo)|Don't Mess With Me!]] and [[Itchy Riches (Combo)|Itchy Ritches]], or [[Paranormal Activity (Combo)|Paranormal Activity]], to have a gigantic boost in your Wallet at the start. His other combo with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Take a Bow (Combo)|Take a Bow]], gives a "Knockback Effect UP (Sm)", which boosts knockback distance. As you are already very likely to be using Tank Cat, it's best to put Kubilan in the first row to boost his ability.

==='''True Form'''===
E. Kubilan Pasalan is no longer used for Crowd Control. Instead, his guaranteed Critical Hits can wipe many weak Metals into utter oblivion. His prime targets include [[Metal Doge]], [[Metal One Horn]] and [[Koronium]], all of which are relevant and can be dangerous if given the chance. However, he will require support as his low DPS means he has no hopes of fighting off tougher ones like [[Super Metal Hippoe]] and [[Sir Metal Seal]]. That being said, his True Form is only worth getting if an Anti-Metal specialist is needed.

Do note that E. Kubilan Pasalan can be a death sentence in some stages, particularly [[Bionic Seaweed]] - His attacks will nuke all the [[Metal Doge]]s, freeing up the enemy limit for bigger threats.

==='''Talents'''===
E. Kubilan Pasalan's talent highlights include '''Wave Immune''' and '''Slow'''. Wave Immune greatly improves his matchups against Wave Metals like Koronium/Cyberface, as well as stages that combine both types of threats. Slow is rather expensive and requires a massive amount of NP for its mediocre effect, but proves to be very helpful when needed by impeding strong Metals that can survive Kubilan's attack.

E. Kubilan, however, doesn't benefit from any of the remaining talents. Attack Buff is useless, as a small damage increase won't meaningfully affect his performance. Meanwhile, HP Buff and Resist Surge are all completely useless due to a combination of low health, the lack of Metal Surge threats and how Surges often deal extreme damage.

