==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Kubiluga was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Legend of the Nekoluga (Removed Combo)|Legend of the Nekoluga]] and [[Nekoluganomicon (Removed Combo)|Nekoluganomicon]].
*Like [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Asiluga]] and [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Balaluga]], Kubiluga's initial form has higher DPS than both of his other forms.
*Kubiluga is the only Nekoluga whose True Form is not a direct upgrade to its evolved form.
*E. Kublian Pasalan calls it a sumo "wrester" instead of a sumo wrestler.
*E. Kubilan Pasalan was the first Cat Unit to have both Wave Attack and Critical Hit abilities.
*This Cat's Evolved Form has the 2nd lowest DPS out of all Ubers in the game, only behind [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Balaluga]].
*Among Nekoluga family, his name Kubi(首)-luga already reflecting that his neck is the part that's abnormally long.
*E. Kubilan Pasalan, according to his name, description, and design (most notably the hairstyle and clothing), is based off of [[wikia:streetfighter:E. Honda|E. Honda]] from the fighting game series ''Street Fighter''. Fittingly, E. Kubilan Pasalan attacks with a headbutt, just like E. Honda.
**Coincidentally, [[E. Honda (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Honda]] himself would later be added to the game as a collaboration exclusive unit.
*Kubiluga's appearance may be based on [[wikipedia:Rokurokubi|Rokurokubi]], a type of yokai with a long neck.

